plicated inbox-parsing logic\n\nThe same \"count captures in `raw/inbox.md`\" logic is duplicated verbatim in two places (`00 JARVIS/🤖 JARVIS.md:131-132` and `output/query_results.md:30-31`). Since Dataview supports `dv.view()` to call a shared script, extract it once:\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Scripts/inbox_count.js\nconst bruto = await dv.io.load(\"raw/inbox.md\");\ndv.container.dataset.count = bruto ? bruto.split(\"\\n\").filter(l => l.trim().startsWith(\"- \") || l.trim().startsWith(\"* \")).length : 0;\n```\nThen in both notes: `dv.view(\"70 Sistema/Scripts/inbox_count\")`. Avoids drift if the capture-line format changes (e.g. tasks with `- [ ]` aren't currently counted — a correctness bug riding along with the duplication).\n\n## Bottom line\nThere's no meaningful backend/frontend performance surface to optimize here — this is a documentation vault. If you meant to point me at a different, actual application codebase (maybe something outside this vault, or a subproject not yet committed), let me know the path and I'll redo this analysis properly against real N+1/React/caching/leak patterns.\n",
